WEBVTT

00:01.680 --> 00:03.390
For now, make yourselves at home.

00:04.020 --> 00:06.900
Not that it's my home either.

00:06.900 --> 00:09.110
I'll have some tea and snacks served.

00:09.350 --> 00:10.820
<i>Oh, my! Snacks!</i>

00:11.190 --> 00:13.240
I appreciate the gesture,

00:13.240 --> 00:15.490
but I don't imagine there's
 an abundance of time.

00:16.050 --> 00:18.030
Let's get straight to the matter at hand.

00:18.370 --> 00:21.020
My, what impressive intensity.

00:21.020 --> 00:23.880
As I would expect of 
His Highness Sion Sol Sunkland.

00:24.780 --> 00:25.960
Sion?!

00:25.960 --> 00:28.630
The prince of Sunkland?

00:28.940 --> 00:30.630
You know who I am?

00:30.630 --> 00:32.200
But of course.

00:32.200 --> 00:37.320
Otherwise, I wouldn't have permitted you 
to remain armed as I led you here.

00:37.990 --> 00:44.520
So, why did you lead us here when we're 
potential obstacles to the revolution?

00:44.870 --> 00:47.980
We have hopes of receiving 
support from your kingdom.

00:47.980 --> 00:50.430
Don't speak of it so lightly.

00:50.430 --> 00:53.440
Mobilizing the military is 
a major national matter.

00:54.580 --> 00:58.660
That statement is out of character for 
someone who so prizes justice and fairness.

00:59.100 --> 01:01.840
Even assuming my kingdom would support you,

01:01.840 --> 01:05.940
there's no guarantee you 
can hold out until then.

01:06.290 --> 01:11.380
This is halfway between the capital 
and Count Donovan's lands.

01:11.660 --> 01:12.880
In other words...

01:13.330 --> 01:16.640
You mean to divide the 
Adamant Infantry from the capital.

01:17.110 --> 01:19.250
You'll hit their supply line.

01:21.380 --> 01:23.770
<i>Even if their direct route 
to the capital is cut off,</i>

01:23.770 --> 01:25.930
<i>they're still in their own country.</i>

01:25.930 --> 01:28.520
<i>They can get supplies from nearby.</i>

01:29.180 --> 01:31.590
<i>But it would take time to arrange that.</i>

01:32.330 --> 01:35.940
<i>Some temporary confusion and disarray 
among the soldiers would be inevitable.</i>

01:36.700 --> 01:41.240
<i>If he stirred a rebellion in this 
town in anticipation of that...</i>

01:42.420 --> 01:44.500
<i>then this man is not to be taken lightly.</i>

01:44.900 --> 01:49.050
<i>Sion's wariness of Lambert went up a level.</i>

01:49.050 --> 01:51.840
<i>Mia, meanwhile...</i>

01:55.050 --> 01:59.050
<i>These cookies... Not only are they 
beautiful, but they're delicious, too!</i>

01:59.760 --> 02:02.510
<i>This man is quite good.</i>

02:03.050 --> 02:04.720
<i>He's not to be taken lightly!</i>

02:05.200 --> 02:09.490
<i>Miraculously, their opinions aligned.</i>

03:39.990 --> 03:49.950
Capital

03:40.990 --> 03:45.250
<i>Remno could truly boast two things 
in comparison to other nations:</i>

03:41.990 --> 03:53.920
Xenia

03:45.250 --> 03:48.990
<i>The vast highways set up within the kingdom,</i>

03:48.040 --> 03:53.920
Donovan

03:48.990 --> 03:53.920
<i>and a military with high mobility 
predicated on those roads.</i>

03:54.250 --> 03:58.920
<b>Episode 11: A Reunion, a Duel, and...</b>

03:54.510 --> 03:58.080
<i>If one were to strengthen it further...</i>

03:59.960 --> 04:02.890
Forces planned for invasion 
of other nations...

04:03.540 --> 04:06.630
So that's what the heavy 
taxes were levied for.

04:06.890 --> 04:09.870
However, the royal government deployed

04:09.870 --> 04:15.470
the excessively powerful
 Adamant Infantry to suppress the people.

04:18.320 --> 04:21.040
<i>There are a variety of 
circumstances at play, but...</i>

04:21.040 --> 04:23.400
<i>After levying heavy taxes on the people,</i>

04:23.400 --> 04:25.940
<i>they imprisoned the vassal 
who spoke for the people.</i>

04:26.350 --> 04:30.480
<i>Isn't that on its own enough 
to be considered unfit to rule?</i>

04:31.630 --> 04:34.970
<i>I only intended to come as 
Princess Mia's escort. But now...</i>

04:44.610 --> 04:47.110
<i>I almost let myself get carried away.</i>

04:49.610 --> 04:52.630
<i>Prince Sion should be made an ally,</i>

04:52.630 --> 04:57.840
<i>but Jem said Princess Mia 
might obstruct the revolution.</i>

05:00.800 --> 05:04.170
<i>I need to have Princess Mia
 keep her mouth shut.</i>

05:06.320 --> 05:09.510
I imagine you've had an
 eventful day and must be tired.

05:09.510 --> 05:11.690
You can stay the night here if you like.

05:12.160 --> 05:16.150
I can't say it measures up to a palace, 
but there is a large bath and beds.

05:16.640 --> 05:18.610
Oh, my! A bath!

05:19.110 --> 05:21.140
<i>In the end, she's just a child.</i>

05:21.140 --> 05:23.450
<i>She seems easy enough to coax.</i>

05:23.770 --> 05:26.030
<i>A correct calculation to make.</i>

05:27.460 --> 05:31.250
Don't you think that was a 
careless decision, Princess Mia?

05:31.250 --> 05:33.640
Why, whatever do you mean?

05:34.550 --> 05:38.470
Since they're angling for 
Sunkland's military assistance,

05:38.470 --> 05:41.190
I imagine they won't harm you.

05:41.680 --> 05:45.400
But still, that doesn't mean 
it's wise to stay the night.

05:45.400 --> 05:46.500
Oh, my.

05:46.500 --> 05:47.860
Is something wrong, Princess Mia?

05:50.130 --> 05:54.830
For Remno shampoo,
 this lathers somewhat poorly.

05:55.160 --> 06:00.080
I suppose this means the one
Prince Abel gave me was special.

06:00.510 --> 06:04.050
You really are an imperial princess.

06:04.300 --> 06:07.390
Incidentally, what was 
the name of the shampoo?

06:07.390 --> 06:09.820
I don't remember the name,

06:09.820 --> 06:13.450
but I remember it had an
adorable image of a horse on it.

06:15.230 --> 06:16.560
That's...

06:16.810 --> 06:19.270
It was a very nice shampoo.

06:19.870 --> 06:21.660
Oh, I... see.

06:22.440 --> 06:25.370
That's... wonderful...

06:25.370 --> 06:27.660
<i>Lynsha decided to say nothing.</i>

06:31.700 --> 06:34.980
This mushroom stew is delicious.

06:35.920 --> 06:37.920
Lord Lambert! Emergency!

06:41.630 --> 06:44.720
<i>I didn't imagine the situation 
would progress so quickly.</i>

06:46.480 --> 06:48.660
Did something happen?

06:48.910 --> 06:51.630
I just received a report from my comrades.

06:51.630 --> 06:54.790
The royal government's military has been 
deployed to a fortress on the highway.

06:54.790 --> 06:57.000
Royal government...

06:58.090 --> 07:01.840
The one leading them is the 
second prince, Abel Remno.

07:02.340 --> 07:04.560
Oh, my! Prince Abel!

07:05.470 --> 07:08.810
<i>I'm so glad I got to take a bath yesterday!</i>

07:09.670 --> 07:13.230
If a member of the royal family
 is personally leading,

07:13.230 --> 07:16.080
the objective is to rouse 
the Adamant Infantry.

07:17.950 --> 07:21.750
So that's the path you've 
chosen, Prince Abel?

07:24.760 --> 07:27.260
Mia, you want to go there, right?

07:27.790 --> 07:30.510
What? Uh, no, but...

07:30.510 --> 07:33.380
Well, even if you aren't going, I am.

07:33.960 --> 07:38.590
In fact, it would probably make things 
easier if you didn't come along.

07:38.590 --> 07:40.800
Huh? Why?

07:41.130 --> 07:44.160
I have some things I need to ask Prince Abel.

07:45.000 --> 07:45.980
Depending his answers...

07:46.880 --> 07:51.490
I may have to carry out what 
I mentioned to you the other night.

07:56.520 --> 08:02.240
I can't just sit back and watch 
the populace get slaughtered.

08:04.250 --> 08:07.160
Are you... going to kill Prince Abel?

08:08.240 --> 08:10.870
I hope I won't have to.

08:11.370 --> 08:14.140
<i>I don't want Prince Abel to die.</i>

08:14.140 --> 08:16.580
<i>And of course I don't want 
Prince Sion to, either.</i>

08:17.110 --> 08:18.270
<i>Most of all,</i>

08:18.270 --> 08:22.250
<i>I don't want them to try to kill each other 
while I have no idea what's going on!</i>

08:25.600 --> 08:26.800
Prince Sion!

08:28.750 --> 08:29.850
I, too..

08:30.230 --> 08:32.610
I, too, shall glow!

08:35.300 --> 08:37.010
<i>Mia messed up the delivery!</i>

08:40.630 --> 08:45.170
Tell me, are you of a 
mind to work with us now?

08:47.390 --> 08:54.080
I don't consider His Majesty to 
have made a decisive mistake, Jem.

08:55.080 --> 09:00.220
I shall explain every way I can 
until he heeds my protest.

09:01.130 --> 09:05.980
I am not so naïve as to succumb to 
some strange man's enticements.

09:09.270 --> 09:11.440
Prince, what is your decision?

09:11.890 --> 09:15.450
I see no reason to give them any more time.

09:15.820 --> 09:18.740
Fortunately, the walls of Xenia are low,

09:18.740 --> 09:22.240
and the barricades the rebels built are weak.

09:22.760 --> 09:25.110
It should not prove difficult to breach.

09:27.970 --> 09:30.840
My duty as prince...

09:31.840 --> 09:34.050
Report! Movement in the city!

09:34.220 --> 09:35.760
Have they sent a messenger?

09:36.050 --> 09:41.590
No, but you see, two kids showed up and 
are seeking an audience with Prince Abel.

09:41.590 --> 09:42.930
Foolish.

09:42.930 --> 09:46.440
For rebel elements to dare seek 
an audience with His Highness...

09:46.650 --> 09:49.830
Uh, well, sir, they're not just any kids.

09:49.830 --> 09:52.590
They say they're His Highness's schoolmates.

09:53.200 --> 09:54.260
Excuse me.

09:57.080 --> 10:00.130
Prince Sion! Why are you here?

10:00.130 --> 10:02.830
Hold on. Don't tell me that means...

10:08.180 --> 10:10.790
It's been a long time, Prince Abel.

10:11.280 --> 10:12.410
Princess Mia!

10:13.220 --> 10:17.010
If you had come to see me, I'd be overjoyed.

10:17.010 --> 10:21.460
Oh? What other reason should 
there be for me to come here?

10:22.740 --> 10:26.390
<i>It might be true that she came to see me.</i>

10:27.000 --> 10:32.460
<i>But I'm sure her greater purpose 
is to settle this foolish conflict.</i>

10:34.020 --> 10:37.920
<i>I imagine Princess Mia probably 
wouldn't take my side in this...</i>

10:38.860 --> 10:40.690
<i>Still, I must...</i>

10:42.090 --> 10:44.860
What about you, Prince Sion?

10:47.460 --> 10:53.790
I don't expect you'll say the same as 
Princess Mia, that you came to see me.

10:53.790 --> 10:58.900
No. I originally intended 
only to guard Princess Mia.

10:59.540 --> 11:02.140
But with things having gone this far, 
I can't just stay silent.

11:03.780 --> 11:06.360
It's a little sooner than I'd imagined,

11:07.130 --> 11:11.230
but I think I'll fulfill the 
promise I made for a rematch.

11:11.670 --> 11:12.330
What?

11:14.220 --> 11:18.780
Does that mean you're 
challenging me to a duel?

11:19.070 --> 11:21.280
Pay him no mind!

11:21.280 --> 11:25.740
Prince Abel, a prince leading an army 
needn't participate in single combat.

11:26.620 --> 11:28.170
Stand down, Bernard.

11:28.640 --> 11:35.750
The prince of Sunkland has challenged me to 
a duel in pursuit of his view of justice!

11:36.470 --> 11:40.450
Should I refuse him, 
it will affect the troops' morale.

11:41.080 --> 11:45.420
<i>Besides, I can't back down with her watching.</i>

11:46.100 --> 11:49.510
Prince Sion, I accept your challenge.

11:50.330 --> 11:53.480
<i>Wh-What? That's strange...</i>

11:53.830 --> 11:59.010
<i>I did say that I came
 to see Prince Abel, right?</i>

11:59.010 --> 12:03.840
<i>In all the stories, 
isn't this the part where they hug,</i>

12:03.840 --> 12:10.100
<i>and then the mood changes, 
and everything gets solved?</i>

12:14.330 --> 12:17.500
Bernard, I'm giving you a special order.

12:18.040 --> 12:21.530
Stay at Princess Mia's side and protect her.

12:21.530 --> 12:22.860
Prince Abel!

12:23.600 --> 12:29.890
We'll need the princess to serve as 
witness that our duel was proper.

12:30.070 --> 12:32.390
Don't do this! Don't duel!

12:32.740 --> 12:36.550
I wish we could have enjoyed 
our reunion more...

12:37.230 --> 12:38.110
I wish...

12:41.540 --> 12:44.360
I sound so full of regret.

12:44.720 --> 12:46.320
Prince Abel!

12:49.980 --> 12:52.500
Did Mia's words not get through to you?

12:52.940 --> 12:56.640
No matter who asks, I cannot stop.

12:57.070 --> 12:59.420
You ought to understand my position.

13:00.070 --> 13:02.920
You'll sacrifice yourself for 
a rotten royal authority?

13:03.330 --> 13:06.140
Even if it is rotten, the royal 
authority is still necessary.

13:06.560 --> 13:11.140
A world without order will wind up bringing 
even greater suffering to the masses.

13:11.670 --> 13:17.600
If the authority is as corrupt as you say,
 then my role is to correct it.

13:21.190 --> 13:25.120
If you intend to aid in the 
oppression of your people,

13:26.040 --> 13:28.530
then fall before my sword.

13:46.800 --> 13:49.260
<i>Such force, even without perfect form.</i>

13:52.590 --> 13:57.440
I see I wasn't the only one 
training for our rematch.

13:57.670 --> 14:00.400
I have to surpass a prodigy.

14:01.000 --> 14:03.650
That requires putting in the effort!

14:06.630 --> 14:08.200
Wh-Who are you people?

14:22.500 --> 14:25.440
You get out of range by 
closing in even further, eh?

14:25.440 --> 14:27.630
You're good, Abel Remno.

14:27.890 --> 14:31.860
Likewise. You don't disappoint, Prince Sion.

14:40.910 --> 14:42.360
I-Incredible...

14:43.020 --> 14:45.750
<i>The force of his strikes is increasing.</i>

14:45.750 --> 14:49.100
<i>Has he been adjusting the range as he fights?</i>

14:49.100 --> 14:51.090
<i>That's a prodigy for you.</i>

14:53.660 --> 14:55.160
<i>I can't hold out any longer...</i>

14:55.990 --> 15:01.000
<i>But I can't let her see 
me looking disgraceful.</i>

15:02.350 --> 15:04.770
Assume your stance, Prince Sion.

15:04.770 --> 15:06.130
This will be our final clash.

15:12.220 --> 15:14.270
Please, stop this already!

15:14.270 --> 15:17.850
You'll both really die!

15:24.180 --> 15:28.750
<i>In the end, my words don't 
get through to them.</i>

15:29.140 --> 15:29.600
Buzz off!

15:29.600 --> 15:30.610
Stupid girl!

15:30.610 --> 15:34.770
All of you, please! Listen 
to what I have to say!

15:38.720 --> 15:41.050
<i>It's just like back then...</i>

15:41.520 --> 15:45.710
<i>Before someone who has picked up 
a sword and resolved to fight,</i>

15:45.710 --> 15:47.770
<i>words are ultimately powerless.</i>

15:48.730 --> 15:51.250
Sion. Prince Abel...

15:51.250 --> 15:52.630
<i>Is that true?</i>

15:52.630 --> 15:55.390
I'm begging you. Please...

15:55.910 --> 16:00.770
<i>Will Mia's entreaties, her pleas, 
really reach no one?</i>

16:01.410 --> 16:02.280
<i>No!</i>

16:02.280 --> 16:04.080
Don't die!

16:04.470 --> 16:05.800
<i>That's not what happens!</i>

16:06.400 --> 16:10.520
<i>Even though Mia's pleas have failed 
to reach the combat-locked princes,</i>

16:10.520 --> 16:14.320
<i>the bonds she forged will 
carry her wishes through!</i>

16:16.030 --> 16:17.990
<i>But to who?</i>

16:22.720 --> 16:25.640
<i>To her reliable, loyal retainers!</i>

16:29.760 --> 16:31.230
We can't have this.

16:37.670 --> 16:41.390
Don't you think your mischief 
has gone a bit too far, my princes?

16:42.470 --> 16:47.840
Our princess is a crybaby, so might 
I ask you not to distress her too much?

16:47.840 --> 16:49.080
Mr. Dion...

16:49.380 --> 16:54.780
Knave! How dare you ruin a 
sacred duel between royalty!

16:56.600 --> 16:58.160
Yeah, I get your point.

16:58.560 --> 17:01.510
As a retainer, you've been enduring 
the risk to your prince,

17:01.510 --> 17:03.760
so I suppose you don't like me butting in.

17:04.300 --> 17:09.210
But you see, the one I pledged my 
sword to is neither of His Highnesses.

17:09.210 --> 17:12.460
Silence! Your affront 
shall be met with death!

17:24.720 --> 17:26.560
You cut iron?!

17:27.600 --> 17:31.230
Well, my lord is watching, 
so I need to perform.

17:34.480 --> 17:36.900
Both of you, that's quite enough!

17:39.280 --> 17:40.620
Anne!

17:41.330 --> 17:44.040
Princess Mia, I'm so glad you're safe.

17:47.570 --> 17:49.570
Anne!

17:49.570 --> 17:52.500
Anne! Anne!

17:53.110 --> 17:56.340
Enough! You are in Her Highness 
Princess Mia's presence!

17:56.680 --> 17:59.300
Both of you, put down your weapons at once!

18:00.880 --> 18:05.270
<i>This was superb and ingenious 
stage-setting by Ludwig.</i>

18:05.690 --> 18:09.480
<i>After overwhelming the mighty knight Bernard,</i>

18:09.480 --> 18:13.190
<i>Dion obediently complied 
and put down his sword,</i>

18:13.470 --> 18:17.920
<i>thus placing Mia firmly in 
charge of the situation.</i>

18:18.360 --> 18:19.080
Huh?

18:19.550 --> 18:23.370
<i>Why is everyone looking at me?</i>

18:24.110 --> 18:28.580
<i>Go on. The rest lies with you, Your Highness.</i>

18:28.580 --> 18:29.510
<i>What?!</i>

18:29.510 --> 18:33.290
<i>Don't tell me they're expecting a speech...</i>

18:34.240 --> 18:36.170
We're right by your side.

18:36.170 --> 18:38.760
<i>They </i>are<i> expecting one?</i>

18:41.720 --> 18:44.870
<i>Th-This is kinda scary!</i>

18:54.440 --> 18:56.870
Everyone, lend me your ears!

18:57.450 --> 19:00.750
I am Mia Lunya Tearmew—!

19:03.370 --> 19:05.550
<i>Mia bit her tongue.</i>

19:06.160 --> 19:09.760
<i>Her eyes were slightly wet 
with tears from the pain.</i>

19:11.510 --> 19:13.880
<i>She just captured the 
soldiers' hearts with that!</i>

19:14.120 --> 19:15.890
I can't take it!

19:15.890 --> 19:17.850
Princess Mia, you can do it!

19:18.720 --> 19:22.900
<i>Hey, wait. What am I supposed to talk about?</i>

19:22.900 --> 19:26.300
<i>Mia has no plan to stop Remno's army.</i>

19:26.300 --> 19:31.370
<i>To begin with, the whole reason 
Mia came this far was to see Abel.</i>

19:31.370 --> 19:34.810
<i>Wh-Wh-What do I do?</i>

19:35.150 --> 19:39.660
<i>F-For now, I better... I better 
start saying something!</i>

19:43.920 --> 19:45.870
Soldiers of the Remno army,

19:46.400 --> 19:51.180
I ask that you return to the capital 
without ever drawing your swords.

19:51.470 --> 19:56.500
Absurd! You're telling us to do nothing 
about the rebels and just turn back?

19:57.660 --> 20:00.080
<i>He's scary!</i>

20:00.080 --> 20:05.470
<i>Due to Bernard's intensity,
 Mia's brain finally kicked into gear.</i>

20:06.270 --> 20:11.100
I-It's ridiculous, after all! 
For you to fight.

20:11.100 --> 20:17.820
<i>"Your opponents are rabble. Not worth 
engaging for such fine knights as yourselves."</i>

20:17.820 --> 20:23.870
<i>Mia hit them with this, 
her best, full-power shot.</i>

20:23.870 --> 20:25.500
Ridiculous, huh...

20:26.670 --> 20:32.680
That reminds me. You said something
 curious before, that something felt off?

20:32.680 --> 20:35.750
That's right. I did say that!

20:36.310 --> 20:39.600
<i>I mean, what I've seen in the 
Kingdom of Remno is completely different</i>

20:39.600 --> 20:44.200
<i>from the situation the 
Tearmoon Empire was in before.</i>

20:44.200 --> 20:45.730
<i>And yet...</i>

20:46.140 --> 20:49.970
<i>Outland Count Rudolvon 
and Chancellor Donovan.</i>

20:49.970 --> 20:54.080
<i>Civil war arises due to harm to 
aristocratic allies of the people.</i>

20:54.080 --> 20:55.470
<i>And in both cases,</i>

20:55.470 --> 20:59.710
<i>it's Sunkland that swoops in to save 
the people suffering under tyranny.</i>

21:00.300 --> 21:04.570
<i>A coincidence like that in two places 
with completely different conditions...</i>

21:04.570 --> 21:06.450
<i>It doesn't add up at all!</i>

21:07.010 --> 21:13.720
<i>It's as if somebody is setting things up 
to make Sunkland executors of justice.</i>

21:14.180 --> 21:15.670
<i>That's it.</i>

21:16.650 --> 21:18.930
This appears to be a cunning plot.

21:19.890 --> 21:23.730
<i>Oh? But how do I explain this?</i>

21:23.730 --> 21:26.580
<i>I can't afford to explain 
the previous timeline.</i>

21:26.580 --> 21:29.100
<i>Um... Um...</i>

21:29.520 --> 21:31.500
A cunning plot...

21:31.910 --> 21:38.260
Your Highness, you mean this rebellion was 
designed by someone to divide our nation,

21:38.260 --> 21:43.750
and that to be puppeted into killing 
our fellow countrymen is ridiculous?

21:43.750 --> 21:45.340
Is that what you mean to suggest?

21:46.400 --> 21:47.060
Huh?

21:48.510 --> 21:53.760
And could that also be why Prince Sion 
risked himself to stop Prince Abel?

21:53.760 --> 21:54.840
No, I—

21:55.920 --> 21:59.570
You came here to protect me,

21:59.570 --> 22:04.450
so if my objective is to 
stop this cunning plot,

22:04.450 --> 22:08.130
then is it not fair to say at least 
half of why you came was that?

22:08.130 --> 22:10.030
It is, isn't it?

22:10.030 --> 22:12.900
Well I suppose it wouldn't be entirely 
inaccurate to put it that way...

22:14.640 --> 22:18.560
<i>Well, how was that? That got us 
out of this situation, didn't it?</i>

22:21.120 --> 22:26.550
Your Highness, I'm afraid that 
even if we assume this to be true,

22:26.550 --> 22:32.160
it doesn't change the fact that we must 
dismantle the rebel army and restore order.

22:34.480 --> 22:37.980
Since the taxes will not be lowered,

22:37.980 --> 22:41.330
I do not believe they will put 
down their weapons so easily.

22:42.720 --> 22:49.300
You're mistaken. The aim of the uprising 
is to demand Count Donovan's release.

22:51.000 --> 22:54.740
Prince Abel, have you heard 
anything from His Majesty

22:54.740 --> 22:56.880
about Count Donovan being jailed?

22:56.880 --> 22:59.020
No, this is the first I've heard of it.

22:59.360 --> 23:05.360
Princess Mia, I'm sure you have 
an idea where he's being held,

23:06.160 --> 23:09.240
but don't you think he may 
have already been killed?

23:09.710 --> 23:12.350
Huh? I, well, uh...

23:12.350 --> 23:16.330
It appears <i>I'd</i> better answer that one.

23:18.710 --> 23:21.000
Sorry we're late, everyone.

23:21.420 --> 23:22.880
Lady Tiona!

23:23.280 --> 23:25.590
Keithwood! You're all right!

23:25.850 --> 23:27.810
I bring good news!

23:28.480 --> 23:32.020
Actually, for us, I suppose 
it may be bad news.

23:32.710 --> 23:33.700
Huh?

23:34.970 --> 23:39.980
Illustrated by: Mizu Morino
